{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92474-mummy-celeste","id":92474,"title":"Mummy: Celeste *****","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-16T14:45:46-07:00","id":92474,"title":"Mummy: Celeste *****","content":"I got an idea for a Mummy-game from reading D&amp;D's monster-manual; an ancient and powerful mummy awakens in Egypt during the time of ancient Rome and builds herself an army to the extent, Rome must deal with her. The mummy-queen will be powerful enough to command other less-powerful mummies. If she had powerful level-5 spells like Celeste, should could literally destroy whole cities with an earthquake or cause a drought and a famine. <br /> <br /> The game would probably be Mummy v. Mortal, but other supernaturals could get involved; hedge-magicians might notice a flux in the spirit world from all the mummies' spells. <br /> <br /> Amulet-Factor / &quot;Raise&quot;, an Army: it's conceivable that, the mummy-queen can take some time and produce lots of magical amulets and or, raise an army of the undead (haven't read mummies can do that yet in the spells). She could literally raise an legion given the amount of time she can put into it. Sounds plausible? <br /> <br /> I'm picturing her at an oasis in the Egyptian desert. She has a cult of mortal followers. Perhaps in the eastern-mountains.<br /> <br /> One more question; how can a mummy, look like an undead mummy? In the book, they seem to look alive. I'm thinking of having her look undead, but wear a mask carved from human flesh (Dead-Skin Mask).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T23:08:57-07:00","id":96205,"title":"","content":"Amulets/Raising an Army: Amulets aren't cheap to produce, nor easy, even for a powerful mummy, so providing the numbers necessary to empower an army is nigh impossible. Empowering a retinue of guards? Sure, with time/effort. A proper army/legion? Nope.<br /> <br /> Mummy looking &quot;undead&quot;: easy -- just give her a Flaw to simulate such, either as a sub-class of Reborn who have a particular weakness (like some of the alternate mummies in the back of Resurrection) or as a character-specific imperfection in her creation/soul. I'd call it &quot;Undead Mein&quot;, or &quot;Body of the Dead&quot;, depending on how bad the appearance is: 2pts. if she's got a sunken, pale-undead look about her, or 3-4pts. if she looks outright monstrous and scares most mortals she comes in contact with. Tweak to your own ratings/settings...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}